> > I tested locally and the changes work for me. Both test_alarm and test_alarm_callback work for me.
> > Unrelated to this PR, the time incrementing test appears to set a time with nanoseconds > 1 sec. That seems odd to me. Should I open a ticket or is that supposed to happen?
> 
> I see, the incrementing test is using `timegm` which uses `struct tm`, which has no nanosecond field. so nsec gets a random value

I would think it should be:
```
ZTEST(rtc_api, test_time_counting)
{
	struct rtc_time datetime_set = {0};
	struct rtc_time datetime_get = {0};
```

Also, the AMBIQ does not support `.update_set_callback` so the arch returns with -ENOSYS and the test fails.

```
static inline int z_impl_rtc_update_set_callback(const struct device *dev,
						 rtc_update_callback callback, void *user_data)
{
 	const struct rtc_driver_api *api = (const struct rtc_driver_api *)dev->api;

 	if (api->update_set_callback == NULL) {
 		return -ENOSYS;
 	}

 	return api->update_set_callback(dev, callback, user_data);
}
```

It should be skipped but should it be ENOSYS? or ENOTSUP?

